course: dictionary
lesson: 2139
title: Coordinate: points, places and teamwork
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coordinate has more than one meaning, so context helps you choose. In maths, coordinates are a pair of numbers, like (3, 5), that show exactly where a point is on a grid. On a map, coordinates are latitude and longitude numbers that find a place on the Earth.
explain: As a verb, to coordinate means to organise people or things so they work well together. A team captain coordinates who plays where, so the whole team moves as one.
explain: «The world sets its clocks from Coordinated Universal Time, or UTC.» Coordinated is not used here in the sense of a team. The clue is the word Universal: the whole world uses one agreed time, so the clocks everywhere fit together. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: Coordinate is a noun (a pair of numbers, like (3, 5)) and a verb (to organise things so they work well together).
fact: In maths, the first coordinate goes along, across the grid, and the second goes up.
fact: Latitude and longitude are coordinates that give any place on the Earth.
fact: To coordinate your body is to make your arms, legs and eyes move together smoothly, as in catching a ball.
fact: «Coordinated Universal Time» (UTC) is the agreed time that the world sets its clocks from.
exercise: «The world sets its clocks from Coordinated Universal Time.» Which word in this sentence is a form of coordinate? | Time | *Coordinated | Clocks | Universal
exercise: In maths, the first coordinate is along and the second is up. In the point (3, 5), which way does the 3 tell you to go? | Round in a circle | Up, to the top of the graph | Down, to the bottom of the graph | *Along, across the grid
exercise: Mia's netball team needs someone to coordinate who plays where. What does coordinate mean here? | To count the points at the end | To hit the ball as hard as possible | To lose the match on purpose | *To organise people so they work well together
test: Ella's dance teacher says her arms, legs and eyes must coordinate. What does she mean? | She must dance alone | *Her arms, legs and eyes move together smoothly | Her arms must be longer than her legs | She should stop dancing
test: On a map, what do latitude and longitude coordinates give? | The name of the river | *A place on the Earth | The weather for next week | The speed of a car
exam: «The world sets its clocks from Coordinated Universal Time.» What does the word Universal suggest about this time? | It is a kind of sport | *It is the same for the whole world | It changes every hour | It is only for one school
